<title>ESTONIA: NORMA IN MAIN LIST BID.</title>
<headline>NORMA IN MAIN LIST BID.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonian industrial concern Norma, which is currently traded on the free market of the country's bourse, said on Friday that it was seeking to be included on the main list in two months' time.  </p>
<p>&quot;Norma's council has made a principled decision to have its shares placed on the main list of the Tallinn stock exchange,&quot; Juri Kao, the chairman of the company's council, said at the shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>Norma's shares have been traded on the free market since August of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom +372 6 30 84 00</p>
